The '''2014 Football League Cup final''' was a [[association football|football]] match that took place on 2 March 2014 at [[Wembley Stadium]], London. It was the final match of the [[2013–14 Football League Cup]], the 54th season of the [[EFL Cup|Football League Cup]], a football competition for the 92 teams in the [[Premier League]] and [[English Football League|The Football League]].

The match was contested by Premier League clubs [[Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]] and [[Sunderland A.F.C|Sunderland]]. Manchester City appeared in their fourth League Cup final, and made their sixth Wembley visit since 2011.<ref>{{cite news |title=West Ham 0–3 Man City |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/25723655 |publisher=BBC Sport (British Broadcasting Corporation) |date=21 January 2014 |access-date=21 January 2014 }}</ref><ref>{{cite news|title=League Cup Past Winners |url=http://www.football-league.co.uk/page/LeagueCupPastWinners/0,,10794~1354853,00.html |work=The Football League |date=24 February 2013 |access-date=21 January 2014 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131203092702/http://www.football-league.co.uk/page/LeagueCupPastWinners/0%2C%2C10794~1354853%2C00.html |archive-date=3 December 2013 }}</ref> Sunderland appeared in their second League Cup final, their first visit to Wembley since 1998 when they lost to [[Charlton Athletic F.C.|Charlton Athletic]] in the First Division play-off final.

By winning the final, Manchester City would have qualified for the third qualifying round of the [[2014–15 UEFA Europa League|2014–15 Europa League]], but they qualified for the Champions League via their [[2013–14 Premier League|league]] position. Thus, the Europa League berth was given to [[Tottenham Hotspur F.C.|Tottenham Hotspur]], the team that finished sixth in the Premier League.<ref>{{cite news |title=Manchester City win League Cup as Touré wonder goal sparks comeback |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/mar/02/manchester-city-sunderland-capital-one-cup-final-match-report |work=The Guardian |publisher=Guardian News and Media |date=2 March 2014 |access-date=3 March 2014 }}</ref>

